**Purchase price: €425,000**  
**Proposed lender: Imaginary Bank DAC**

Dear Alex,

Thank you for instructing Fictional Legal LLP (“the Firm”) in connection with your proposed purchase of the above property.

This letter, together with the Standard Terms of Engagement in Schedule 1, records the basis upon which we will act for you. It also contains information about our professional fees, VAT and anticipated outlays. Please read it carefully and contact us if anything is unclear.

Our engagement will commence when we have received:

1. a signed copy of this letter;
2. satisfactory evidence of your identity and address;
3. the requested information concerning your source of funds and wealth;
4. confirmation that no conflict of interest prevents us from acting; and
5. the initial payment on account referred to below.

## 1. Your solicitor and contact details

The solicitor with primary responsibility for your matter will be:

**Morgan Sample, Solicitor**  
T: +353 (0)1 555 0101  
E: morgan.sample@fictionallegal.example

Morgan Sample will be assisted by members of our residential property team. The supervising partner is **Taylor Placeholder, Partner**.

Our office hours are 9.00 a.m. to 5.30 p.m., Monday to Friday, excluding public holidays.

## 2. Your instructions

You have instructed us to act for you in the purchase of 42 Demonstration Drive, Sampletown, Dublin D00 Z0Z0 for €425,000.

You have informed us that:

- the property is a second-hand residential house;
- you are purchasing it in your sole name as your principal private residence;
- the title is expected to be registered title comprising one folio;
- the transaction is not an auction purchase;
- the purchase is subject to mortgage finance from Imaginary Bank DAC;
- no part of the purchase price is being provided by an undisclosed third party;
- you are not relying on the sale of another property to complete this purchase; and
- there is no unusual tax, probate, family law, insolvency, trust, company or planning issue presently known to you.

You must tell us immediately if any of these assumptions is incorrect or changes.

## 3. Scope of our work

Subject to receiving the necessary documents and instructions, our work will ordinarily include:

1. reviewing the contract for sale, title documents and replies to standard requisitions;
2. raising appropriate pre-contract enquiries with the seller’s solicitor;
3. advising you on the principal legal terms of the contract;
4. investigating the seller’s title to the property;
5. reviewing available planning documents, statutory declarations and compliance certificates furnished by the seller;
6. carrying out the usual conveyancing searches;
7. advising on the legal effect of matters disclosed by the title and searches;
8. dealing with one standard residential mortgage loan offer from Imaginary Bank DAC;
9. explaining the principal terms of the mortgage and arranging execution of the mortgage documents;
10. complying with the lender’s conveyancing requirements, insofar as they are lawful and applicable;
11. arranging the signing and exchange of contracts;
12. preparing for and attending to the legal aspects of completion;
13. receiving and transferring completion funds through our client account;
14. preparing and filing the Stamp Duty return on the basis of information supplied by you;
15. paying Stamp Duty from funds provided by you;
16. lodging the purchase deed and mortgage for registration with Tailte Éireann;
17. dealing with routine registration queries;
18. reporting to you and the lender following completion and registration; and
19. holding the title documentation in accordance with the lender’s requirements.

We will keep you reasonably informed of material developments and will seek your instructions where a decision is required.

## 4. Matters not included

Unless separately agreed in writing, our work does not include:

- a structural survey, valuation, snag list or physical inspection;
- advice on the structural condition, boundaries on the ground, services, flooding, pyrite, mica, radon, contamination or environmental condition of the property;
- verification that planning permissions or building regulations have been complied with as a matter of fact;
- specialist planning, engineering, architectural or environmental advice;
- advice on the adequacy of the Building Energy Rating;
- negotiation of the purchase price or commercial terms;
- tax, accounting, financial, investment, pension or insurance advice, other than routine Stamp Duty matters;
- advice on entitlement to any Stamp Duty refund, relief or exemption unless specifically agreed;
- litigation or dispute resolution;
- rectification of title defects or complex registration applications;
- probate, matrimonial, cohabitation, succession or estate-planning advice;
- advice concerning a co-ownership agreement, declaration of trust or third-party contribution;
